      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I just had a look in the resource monitor: there was indeed a Suspended install.exe process which I had to kill to get my OSC back. It does not show up in task manager at all, only in resource manager, and VRC starts just fine. It just seems like an install.exe process instance gets suspended and never terminates, so it holds the port open forever and ever.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
